    "content": "[PDF PAGE 1]\nFirst Observation\nWatching price being delivered every open and close created.\n\nThis means watching all TFs. TFs are only showing a different representation of the same\nprice data. The amount of time in a candle will change the look of a chart but, remember\nthat it is still a single set of data we are viewing. By observing price delivery, you\nsubconsciously build your interpretation of the consistencies in how price is being\ndelivered.\n\nRather than looking at the market with ideas you have built over time from previous\nlearning (you will subconsciously do this), you can rewire this by following what price\n\n\n\n\n                                                                           e\nactually does and not what you think it will do. Over time you will flow with the market.\nPrice delivery repeats itself.\n\n\n\n\n                                                         ad\nYour goal is to build the skill, being able to know what a H1 candle close looks like and\n                                                       Tr\nmeans while still being on a LTF. This skill will come over time.\n\n   ➔   If it’s 1pm check the H1 close\n                                        tA\n   ➔   1:15pm check the 15min close\n   ➔   2pm check the H4 close.\n   ➔   And so on, check the closes!\n                              us\n\n\nTo start with build a habit of looking up and down TFs & test yourself by thinking in your\nmind what that TF candle will look like (bullish, bearish, doji ,OB ,inefficiency & so on)\n                 J\n\n\n\nTHIS WILL COME OVER TIME SO DON’T FORCE IT.\n              ot\n\n\n\n\n   ➔ Watch price move as it’s happening, don’t try and think, or plot possible POIs. If you can see it with\n     your eyes great, but for now we only need to know the directional bias and wait for price to be\n       N\n\n\n\n\n     delivered.\n   ➔ Focus on London and NY session\n\n\nBe clear-minded during this, anything else is a distraction and you are causing your\nbrain to work harder. Don’t burn out, take a break, go away, come back and\ncontinue to observe price delivery. Remember we are building this skill over time,\nIt’s not going to come overnight.\n\n[PDF PAGE 2]\nSecond Hindsight\nBacktesting ‘live’ data, focusing on the trades that worked out.\n\nSeeing is believing. Watching a trade opportunity unfold and play out after it has happened\ncreates a connection, believing how price is actually delivered (vs how you believe it\nshould be). Leaning from hindsight will be teaching your subconscious what each part of\nthat price delivery means and how to trade it.\n\nRepetition at this stage is very important, once you’ve marked up price delivery over and\nover you will start seeing these moves in real-time as they happen.\n\nOur subconscious loves repetition, the more work you put in at this stage the more likely\n\n\n\n\n                                                                 e\nyou are to notice a trade setting up.\n\n\n\n\n                                                  ad\n   1. Observe a move\n   2. Mark a trade that would have worked out\n   3. Mark the logic supporting the trade\n   4. Understand each detail\n   5. Repeat daily\n                                                Tr\n                                   tA\nThis is exactly how we managed to level up, by observing price being delivered and\nbuilding an understanding of the logic, we then applied this to the live markets in real-time.\nEach week we continue to grow.\n                           us\n\n\nObserve, Understand, Execute.\n                J\n\n\n\nThird The true power m1\n             ot\n\n\n\n\nTo follow on later this week...\n       N"
