    "content": "[PDF PAGE 1]\nSupply and demand trading course\n      Trading tactics\n      Trading tactics example 3\n\n\n  Supply and demand\n\n\n\n\nTrading tactics example 3\nLESSON 58      MODULE 11\n\n\n\nSupply and demand strategy is all about being\ncontrarian and taking setups at the best times,\nand from value areas in the market. I gave you\ndifferent examples to show you how to find\nand trade supply and demand zones. Believe\nme guys, if you can master this method, you\nwill become consistently profitable. Some of\nyou will make lots of money, and others will\nbecome very successful, because you have\nthe same strategy that banks, and financial\ninstitutions use to make money. So, what you\nhave to do is to follow the rules and apply the\nmethod.\n\nRemember guys, this is not a holy grail, this is\na powerful method that will make you money,\nbut you should accept losing some small\ntrades from time to time because you are not a\nbank, you are only using a bank trading\nsystem. And you should know that banks and\nfinancial institution lose some small trades\nfrom time to time as well.\n\nWhat will make a difference between someone\nwho makes money using this strategy and\nsomeone who keeps losing using the same\nmethod is money management. This is why I\nalways recommend you guys to adopt a strict\nmoney management, because without it, you\nwill not make money in the long term.\n\nLet me now share with you another trading\nexample to help you better understand the\nsteps that you should follow to trade a supply\nand demand zone. let’s look at the chart\nexample below:\n\n\n\n\nBy analyzing the USD CHF H4 chart, we can\nsee that there is a strong move that was made\nby sellers, the red candle that formed the\nmove is very big, the beginning of the move is\nquick , and the breakout of the previous\nsupport level confirmed the strength of the\nmove. So, we can see that we are in front of a\nsupply zone.\n\nNow let’s do our top down analysis to see what\nthe market is doing on the higher time frame,\nlook at the weekly USD CHF H4 chart below:\n\n\n\n\nBy analyzing the trend of the higher time\nframe, we can clearly see that the trend is\ndown, and supports our trade on the 4H time\nframe. So, the top down analysis plays in our\nfavor and this gives more strength to our trade\nsetup, because we know now that we will trade\nwith the trend.\n\nThe next step is to draw the supply zone on\nthe 4h time frame and calculate our risk to\nreward ratio, look at the chart below:\n\n\n\n\nAs you can see, to draw the supply zone, we\nidentify the basing candle, and in this case, we\nhave a pin bar as a basing candle. So, we\ndraw a distal line at the upper shadow of the\ncandle, and a proximal line at the lower\nshadow.\n\nWhen drawing the supply zone, we can get an\nidea about our risk, and as you can see, we\nwill not risk too much compared to the reward,\nwe can have at least 1:8 risk to reward ratio.\n\nThe risk to reward ratio of this trade is very\ninteresting, and this is one of the most\nimportant elements that you should take into\nconsideration. Because supply and demand\nzones with low risk to reward ratio will not help\nyou become a winner in the long term. Focus\nalways on trades with at least 1:2 or 1:3 risk to\nreward ratio.\n\nThe last element that we should consider\nbefore entering the market is the candlestick\npattern signal. We need to wait for a\ncandlestick signal, it can be a pin bar, an\ninside bar or an engulfing bar…. look at the\nillustration below to see what happens when\nthe marker reached the supply zone:\n\n\n\n\nAs you can see when prices reached the\nsupply zone, the market was rejected and\nformed a Doji candle, you can enter the market\nafter the close of the Doji. Your stop loss\nshould be placed 10 pips away from the zone\nand the profit target is the next resistance\nlevel.\n\nIf you miss the first Doji, you can enter at the\nclose of the second Doji, and if you miss it as\nwell, you will have another engulfing bar signal\nopportunity, so you place your trade at the\nclose of the engulfing candle, and the stop loss\nabove the supply zone. The profit target is the\nnext resistance level.\n\nThe main goal from sharing these trading\nexamples is to help you master trading supply\nand demand zones by following the easy steps\nthat I mentioned in previous lessons. These\ntrading examples are a reminder of what you\nlearnt in this course. So please if you still find it\ndifficult to identify a supply or a demand zone\non your chart, this is a sign that you were not\nfocused enough when taking the previous\nlessons. So, if you don’t understand\nsomething, you can go back and learn your\nlessons carefully, but if you still have difficulties\nunderstanding something, then you can\ncontact me whenever you want.\n\n\n\n               PREVIOUS LESSON\n\n             NEXT LESSON"
