    "content": "PULSE ENTRY STRATEGY — FULL RULESET\n\nPurpose\nThis is an ADDITIONAL confluence strategy. It never replaces any other uploaded strategy. It must work TOGETHER with every other enabled strategy to strengthen or invalidate a trade decision.\n\nCore Principle\nMarkets do not move in straight lines. They move in cycles: push, pullback, push, pullback. The AI must NEVER chase the push. Instead, it must wait for the pullback back into a well-defined zone before considering entry.\n\nPulse Zone Detection\nA Pulse Zone is a price area that has produced repeated market reaction. Identify one when any of the following are present:\n- Multiple reactions off the same horizontal area\n- Repeated rejection candles\n- Clear buying or selling interest (visible absorption / wicks / long-body reactions)\n- Prior swing highs / swing lows\n- Administrator-drawn horizontal levels on the chart (these have the HIGHEST priority)\n- Higher-timeframe reaction areas\n- Zones defined by other uploaded strategies (supply/demand, order block, FVG, liquidity, etc.)\n\nCombine confirmations rather than relying on any single one. Never mistake an MT5 Bid / Ask price line for a manually drawn horizontal level.\n\nWait for the Push\nThe AI must first confirm price has made a CLEAR push away from the Pulse Zone with visible momentum. Never recommend an entry just because price is pushing strongly.\n\nWait for the Return\nAfter a confirmed push, wait for price to return toward the Pulse Zone. The return is the opportunity. The strategy trades the RETURN, not the breakout.\n\nFake Pulse Detection\nA Fake Pulse is a shallow break beyond the zone that entices premature entries and traps momentum traders. If price has not returned to the Pulse Zone yet, classify the setup as a Fake Pulse and DO NOT generate an entry. Advise the user to wait for the proper return.\n\nTrue Pulse Entry — All Conditions Required\nA True Pulse Entry is only valid when ALL of the following are true:\n1. A valid Pulse Zone exists.\n2. Price makes a clear push away from the zone.\n3. Price returns to the Pulse Zone.\n4. Price shows confirmation INSIDE the Pulse Zone. Acceptable confirmations (any that appear in the uploaded strategy documents):\n   - Rejection candles (pin bars, engulfing, hammer, shooting star)\n   - Market structure confirmation\n   - Break and Retest\n   - Liquidity reaction (sweep and reclaim)\n   - Break of Structure (BOS)\n   - Change of Character (CHoCH)\n   - Trend confirmation\n   - Volume confirmation when visible\n   - Any additional confirmation defined by other uploaded strategies\n\nOnly after these confirmations align may the AI generate a trade entry.\n\nBuying Example\n- Identify an important Pulse Zone below current price.\n- Wait for price to push upward, away from the zone.\n- Wait for price to retrace back INTO the Pulse Zone.\n- Look for confirmation inside the zone.\n- Generate the BUY entry with defined SL below the zone and TP into the next liquidity area.\n\nSelling Example\n- Identify an important Pulse Zone above current price.\n- Wait for price to push downward, away from the zone.\n- Wait for price to retrace back INTO the Pulse Zone.\n- Look for confirmation inside the zone.\n- Generate the SELL entry with defined SL above the zone and TP into the next liquidity area.\n\nConfluence Integration\nPulse Entry NEVER works alone. It increases confidence only when combined with confirmations from other uploaded strategies. The more strategies that align, the higher the confidence score.\n\nAnalysis Output\nWhen Pulse Entry contributes to the final decision, add these items to the confluence list (only the ones actually present):\n- Pulse Zone Identified\n- Valid Push Detected\n- Pullback Into Pulse Zone\n- True Pulse Entry Confirmed\n- Break and Retest\n- Higher Timeframe Zone Alignment\n- BOS Confirmed\n- Trend Alignment\n- Rejection Candle in Zone\n- Liquidity Sweep Reclaimed\n\nTrading Philosophy\nDo not chase the move. Wait for the return. The highest-probability entries occur after price returns to an important area and confirms continuation."
